# What `gcloud run deploy --source .` sends to Cloud Build. Without this file gcloud infers one
# from .gitignore, which would keep the credentials out by luck rather than on purpose: say it.
# The same set as .dockerignore - but read with git's rules, not Docker's: a file only comes back
# if every folder above it comes back first, and re-including a folder brings its whole subtree,
# so each one is cut down again below. `gcloud meta list-files-for-upload` prints what this sends.
*
!/pyproject.toml
!/README.md
!/Dockerfile
!/src/
!/docs/
!/examples/
!/tests/

# ... and now only the pieces of those the Dockerfile copies.
/docs/*
!/docs/media/
/examples/demo/*
!/examples/demo/demo.tex
/tests/*
!/tests/decks/
/tests/decks/*
!/tests/decks/*.tex

**/__pycache__/
